        <div class="prose">
          <h2 id="summary">1. The short version</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>We collect what is needed to sell you jewellery and deliver it. Nothing is collected “just in case”.</li>
            <li>We do not run advertising pixels, we do not build profiles, and we do not sell data to anyone.</li>
            <li>Optional things — analytics counting, marketing email — are <strong>off until you turn them on</strong>.</li>
            <li>You can ask for a copy of your data, correct it, or delete it, and we will tell you exactly what we
              did and what we had to keep.</li>
            <li>We keep invoice records for eight years because tax law requires it. Everything else has a shorter,
              stated lifetime.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 id="who">2. Who is responsible for your data</h2>
          <p>
            The entity responsible (the “data fiduciary” in Indian data-protection language) is
            <strong><%= biz.legalEntity || 'not configured on this deployment' %></strong>, trading as
            <strong><%= biz.tradingName %></strong>.
            <% if (biz.address) { %>Registered / business address: <%= biz.address %>.<% } else { %>
              <span class="env-flag">Registered address not configured</span> — this must be supplied before launch.
            <% } %>
          </p>
          <p>
            Privacy contact: <strong><%= biz.grievanceEmail || biz.email || 'not configured' %></strong>.
            The person named as grievance officer is listed on the <a href="/business-details">business details page</a>.
          </p>

          <h2 id="what">3. What we collect, why, and on what basis</h2>
          <p>
            Each row below is a real field in this system. If a field appears here, it exists in the code; if it is not
            here, we do not collect it.
          </p>
          <table>
            <caption class="sr-only">Personal data collected, its purpose and retention</caption>
            <thead>
              <tr><th scope="col">Data</th><th scope="col">Why we have it</th><th scope="col">Necessary for</th><th scope="col">Kept for</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td>Name</td>
                <td>To address the parcel and the invoice correctly, and to reply to you by name.</td>
                <td>Order fulfilment</td>
                <td>8 years on invoices; profile deleted on request</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Email address</td>
                <td>Order confirmation, delivery updates, replies to support messages, sign-in identity.</td>
                <td>Order fulfilment and account access</td>
                <td>Until account deletion (order records 8 years)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Mobile number</td>
                <td>The courier calls you on delivery day. Nothing else.</td>
                <td>Delivery</td>
                <td>Redacted when the order completes; deleted on request</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Delivery address</td>
                <td>So the parcel reaches you, and to resolve delivery disputes.</td>
                <td>Delivery</td>
                <td>Redacted on deletion; retained on the invoice record</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Order contents and amounts</td>
                <td>Fulfilment, returns, warranty and statutory accounting.</td>
                <td>Contract and tax law</td>
                <td>8 years (tax requirement)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Payment reference and status</td>
                <td>To match your payment to your order and handle refunds. The <em>provider’s</em> reference only —
                  never your card number.</td>
                <td>Contract and tax law</td>
                <td>8 years with the order</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Password (stored only as a one-way scrypt hash)</td>
                <td>To let you sign in. We cannot read it.</td>
                <td>Account security</td>
                <td>Until you change it or delete the account</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Support messages and your replies</td>
                <td>To resolve the issue and keep a record of what was agreed.</td>
                <td>Customer support</td>
                <td>24 months after the last contact</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Reviews you submit</td>
                <td>Published on the product page with a verified-purchase label.</td>
                <td>Consent (you choose to submit)</td>
                <td>Until you ask us to remove it, or the product is delisted</td>
              </tr>
